PipeCraft is an independent runtime dependency. Its source is not vendored in
the Styler repository; architecture-specific Styler release bundles may include
a compiled private PipeCraft binary together with this notice.

PipeCraft owns DAG scheduling, global resource coordination, the lifecycle of
plugin processes, workflow cancellation/events and durable job/resume state.
Styler owns Linux/domain semantics, receipts, backups, reconciliation,
Apply/Undo meaning and the user interface. A Styler domain plugin may still
launch a domain-specific child command (APT, Flatpak, etc.) through Styler's
ProcessRunner; PipeCraft supervises the plugin boundary rather than pretending
to understand those Linux-domain effects itself.

The historical Python scheduler and the former `styler-engine` Rust executable
are not shipped in Styler 0.13.1. Test-only in-process workflow helpers live under
`tests/support` and are excluded from the installed package.
